<p dir="ltr" data-cds-heading=""><strong>What it shows</strong></p>
<ul dir="ltr">
<li><strong>Eight tasks</strong>, in a â€œHAPPENING NOWâ€ section just under the hero. Eight is enough to look busy without pushing the Join buttons down. On a phone you swipe through the cards sideways, and on a computer they sit in a grid.</li>
<li><strong>A mix of categories.</strong> It takes the newest tasks but allows at most two per category, so the cover page doesnâ€™t show eight home repairs in a row.</li>
<li><strong>Each card</strong> shows the category, price, title, general area and how long ago it was posted, with a â€œMake an offerâ€ button. If a task has no price, it says â€œOpen budgetâ€.</li>
<li><strong>A final card</strong> that reads â€œ13 open tasksâ€ (using your real count) with a <strong>Join free</strong> button.</li>
<li><strong>Joining first.</strong> Tapping any card opens the sign-up form, since the full task and map are inside.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="ltr">The section fills itself from your real tasks, so it updates as people post. If there are no open tasks, it stays hidden rather than showing an empty box. Logged-in users never see it.</p>
<p dir="ltr">I tested it with 13 sample tasks at phone and desktop widths. It showed eight cards plus the final one, no more than two per category, and tapping a card opened sign-up with no script errors. I couldnâ€™t test it with your live data.</p>
